<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila Central Bank sells dollars at 26.40 pesos.</title>
<headline>Manila Central Bank sells dollars at 26.40 pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Central Bank confirmed on Monday it was selling dollars at 26.40 pesos.</p>
<p>However, it did not disclose the amount.</p>
<p>Traders said offshore funds were selling pesos after a Singaporean newspaper quoted Finance Secretary Roberto de Ocampo saying the peso may devalue against the dollar.</p>
<p>&quot;I think the Secretary was misquoted,&quot; the central bank official said. &quot;We'll sell as long as there are requirements.&quot;</p>
</text>
